WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Polish subtitles burned into the film.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Tenement houses and monuments. What the sources list as a monument, and how it was checked

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.269
The map shows only objects that a source lists as a monument.

3
00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:14.278
The labels above the map say it plainly: incomplete set, register only from Wikidata.

4
00:00:14.278 --> 00:00:19.289
Kamienica (tenement house) in the atlas: a multi-family building that a source lists as a monument.

5
00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:24.103
Only the construction period is given, never the exact year.

6
00:00:24.103 --> 00:00:29.314
Point locations were checked against the aerial image on a random sample.

7
00:00:29.314 --> 00:00:34.527
The result sits next to the source: on the object, just beside it, off it, with a confidence interval.

8
00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:39.532
Register of monuments: for now only the part in Wikidata, without the NID register.

9
00:00:39.532 --> 00:00:44.544
A missing point does not mean that a building is not a monument.

10
00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:49.929
On the atlas map: register points from Wikidata as a separate layer.

11
00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:54.933
Next to it: the heritage tag in OpenStreetMap. Two sources, two layers.

12
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:59.737
Closer: Stare Miasto.

13
00:00:59.737 --> 00:01:04.741
Sources: Register of monuments: Wikidata (CC0); Heritage tag: © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL); Buildings and complexes: BDOT10k, Główny Urząd Geodezji i Kartografii; District boundaries: © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Full source notes and licences: the „Dane” page.
